; exclude_short_stack_int_register: EXCLUDE pops its operands before it reads its register, so a
; stack one value short raises StackUnderflow even though the register
; would also have been rejected.
;
; spec/xqvm/SPEC.md's error-precedence rule makes operand pops first within
; every instruction. getline_short_stack_int_register pins the rule for
; GETLINE; this vector pins it for the constraints, and
; stack_underflow_beats_a_wrong_typed_register in xqvm/tests/integration.rs
; covers all twenty-two opcodes that name a register and pop. The register
; is filled from calldata rather than left unset, so UnsetRegister cannot
; stand in for the type fault.

PUSH 0
INPUT r0         ; r0 = 5, an int
PUSH 0
PUSH 1
EXCLUDE r0 ; 3 pops, 2 on the stack
HALT
